<%# One picked file: its thumbnail, its title, its alt text, and the remove X.

    ⚠️ **The three fields render in THIS order in every tile.** The names are `files[ids][]`,
    `files[titles][]`, and `files[alts][]`, and the action reads the three arrays by POSITION. A
    tile that omits one field would move each value after it by one.

    ⚠️ The tiles have no order that means anything: one asset does not know about another one.
    Thus this partial has no grip and no drag, and the Social media tile has both.

    ⚠️ Inside a tile the hooks are plain `data-` attributes and NOT Stimulus targets. Only the
    root is a target. That is what lets the <template> of the page clone this markup without two
    elements answering to the same target name. %>
<%# ⚠️ `data-file-alt-url` is the path of the Generate control of THIS tile. The server writes it
    here, and the answer of the upload writes it for a new tile, thus the JavaScript builds no
    path. The control renders only when Claude has a key, and it is disabled while the tile has
    no id. %>
<div class="media-file" data-media-upload-target="file"
     data-file-alt-url="<%= contentful_upload_file_alt_path(file.id) if file.id.present? %>">
  <%# The id that the upload answered with. It is empty while the upload is out, and the action
      drops such a triple. It is first because it renders nothing. %>
  <input type="hidden" name="files[ids][]" value="<%= file.id %>" data-file-id>

  <div class="media-file__media">
    <%# ⚠️ No handler on `error`. A thumbnail that fails to load must not take the file off the
        form: the submit refuses a file that is gone, with a message. %>
    <img class="media-file__image" alt=""
         <% if file.id.present? %>src="<%= contentful_upload_file_path(file.id) %>"<% end %>
         data-file-image>
    <%# It spins while the upload is out. It needs a rule for `[hidden]`; refer to
        _media-upload.scss. %>
    <wa-spinner class="media-file__spinner" data-file-spinner hidden></wa-spinner>
  </div>

  <div class="media-file__text">
    <wa-input class="media-file__title" name="files[titles][]" label="<%= t(".file_title") %>"
              size="small" value="<%= file.title %>" data-file-title>
    </wa-input>

    <wa-textarea class="media-file__alt" name="files[alts][]" label="<%= t(".file_alt") %>"
                 hint="<%= t(".file_alt_hint") %>" rows="3" resize="auto" size="small"
                 value="<%= file.alt %>" data-file-alt>
    </wa-textarea>

    <%# ⚠️ `type="button"`, as each button of a dialog carries: a <wa-button> is form-associated,
        and one with no type in a form could submit the page. The controller sets `loading` and
        `disabled` together while the request is out, thus a second click starts nothing. %>
    <% if alt_text %>
      <wa-button class="media-file__generate" type="button" appearance="outlined" size="small"
                 data-file-generate data-action="click->media-upload#generateAlt"
                 <%= "disabled" if file.id.blank? %>>
        <%= slotted_icon_svg("classic", "light", "sparkles") %>
        <%= t(".generate_alt") %>
      </wa-button>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <wa-button class="media-file__remove" type="button" appearance="plain" size="small"
             data-action="click->media-upload#removeFile">
    <%= raw icon_svg("classic", "light", "circle-xmark") %>
    <span class="wa-visually-hidden"><%= t(".remove_file") %></span>
  </wa-button>
</div>
